        "titolo_orig": "Trump touts Iran inspection deal as Tehran disputes terms",
        "testo_it": "Trump rivendica un accordo sulle ispezioni in Iran, ma Teheran nega la validità dei termini.",
        "priorita": "Alta",
        "id_gruppo": 2,
        "link": "https://www.scmp.com/news/us/article/3358108/trump-touts-iran-inspection-deal-tehran-disputes-terms?utm_source=rss_feed",
        "orario": "18:54",
        "timestamp": 1782233650,
        "contenuto_esteso": "Advertisement US, Israel war on Iran US Trump touts Iran inspection deal as Tehran disputes terms US president says Iran agreed to inspections ‘long into the future’, but Tehran says no decision has been made on IAEA access 2 -MIN READ 2 -MIN Listen Dewey Sim in Washington Published: 12:54am, 24 Jun 2026 US President Donald Trump on Tuesday insisted that Iran has agreed to “highest level” nuclear inspections even as Iranian officials disputed his claim, exposing how much remains contested even with a tentative agreement in place. “Despite their protestations and false statements to the contrary … Iran has fully and completely agreed to highest level Nuclear inspections long into the future (Infinity!!!),” Trump wrote on social media on Tuesday morning. “This will insure ‘Nuclear Honesty.’ If they did not agree to this, there would be no further negotiations!” Trump said he had agreed to keep the strategic Strait of Hormuz open based on this agreement but could reinstate the US naval blockade, even though it was “at this point, highly unlikely”. His comments early on Tuesday came after Iran’s ambassador to the United Nations Ali Bahreini told reporters that Tehran has yet to agree to the deployment of inspectors from the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) to monitor its nuclear activities. He said a working group that has yet to be convened will discuss whether inspectors will travel to Iran. Vance says US-Iran deal will fundamentally transform Middle East Advertisement Select Voice Select Speed 00:00 00:00 1.00"
